---
title: Greek Marinated Chicken
servings: 4
cuisine: greek
main_protein: chicken
prep_time: "15 minutes"
cook_time: "15 minutes"
tags:
  - dinner
image: ../obsidian/attachments/IMG_6376.jpeg
prep:
  - Mince 5 garlic cloves
  - Juice 2 lemons and zest 1 lemon
  - Chop fresh thyme, oregano, rosemary and parsley
  - Clean and oil the grill grates
---

Prepare the marinade. Add all ingredients for the marinade (@olive oil{0.5%cup}, @garlic{5%cloves}, minced, @lemon juice{2%lemons}, @lemon zest{1%lemon}, @fresh thyme{1%tablespoon}, chopped, @fresh oregano{1%tablespoon}, chopped, @fresh rosemary{2%teaspoon}, chopped, @fresh parsley{1%tablespoon}, chopped, @salt{1%teaspoon}, and @black pepper{1%teaspoon}, freshly ground) to a #large shallow mixing bowl{}. Mix well to combine.

Marinate the chicken. Add the @chicken breasts{6} (large, approximately 4 pounds) to the marinade and mix well to coat in the marinade. Allow chicken to marinate for at least ~{30%minutes} to two hours.

Prepare the grill. Clean #grill{} grates and lightly oil with vegetable oil or cooking spray. Set grill to medium-high heat.

Grill the chicken. Remove the chicken from the marinade and place directly on the grill. Discard remaining marinade. Cover the grill and allow chicken to cook for approximately ~{5%minutes} before reducing heat to medium. Allow chicken to cook for an additional ~{2%minutes}, then use #tongs{} to flip each breast over. Grill for an additional ~{5%minutes} (or longer), or until the thickest part of your chicken registers 160 degrees F with a #digital meat thermometer{}.
